llvm-mingw is a cross compiler toolchain targeting Windows, built from
LLVM/Clang, MinGW-w64 headers and runtime libraries, libc++ and
compiler-rt.

The toolchain supports the following Windows targets:

  i686-w64-mingw32
  x86_64-w64-mingw32
  aarch64-w64-mingw32
  armv7-w64-mingw32

Unlike the upstream release builds, this port does not build its own
copy of LLVM.  It uses the clang, lld and LLVM binary utilities from
devel/llvm23 and only builds the MinGW-w64 sysroots and the C/C++
runtime libraries for the Windows targets.
